        "v": [
          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data, and — because `execute = TRUE` — **actually ran it**. We examined 1 R code file.",
          "#### Run order",
          "The scripts were ordered by their data dependencies (a script writing a file another reads runs first), `source()` calls, and numeric filename prefixes.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1L, File = \"needs_stringr.R\", \"Runs after\" = \"—\", \n    Basis = \"none\"), row.names = c(NA, -1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "Every data path in the code works in the repository as deposited.",
          "#### Execution",
          "**The code was run.** Each script ran in an isolated subprocess against a throwaway copy of the repository, in the run order above, with a 60-second per-script timeout. Of 1 script: 1 ran without error, 0 errored, 0 timed out, 0 could not run because one of its own dependencies is unavailable, 0 did not parse. Running against current package versions: a break can reflect version drift, which argues for pinning versions. \n\n*a script hit a `could not find function \"...\"` error; we added the `library()` calls it needs (see below), and re-ran once. The outcomes above are from that corrected run.*",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"needs_stringr.R\", Outcome = \"ran_ok\", \n    Detail = \"\", \"Time (s)\" = 0), row.names = c(NA, -1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "**`library()` calls added**",
          "**1 script uses functions from packages it does not load itself.** The packages are usually loaded in another script of the project, which only helps when the scripts run in one R session in the right order. To run it we added the `library()` calls below at the top. Any such script that then ran is **reproducible only after adding `library()` calls it should make itself**.",
          "Reproducible after adding `library()` calls: needs_stringr.R.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"needs_stringr.R\", \"library() calls added\" = \"library(stringr)\"), row.names = \"needs_stringr.R\", class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "*Expand a row below to see the output each script produced.*",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — needs_stringr.R (ran_ok)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> library(stringr)\n> x <- c(\"apple\", \"banana\")\n> print(str_detect(x, \"an\"))\n[1] FALSE  TRUE\n````\n\n:::\n"
